What: wmediumd, the mac80211_hwsim medium simulator (positions, path loss,
per-link error probability, interference). A test tool: it runs beside
mac80211_hwsim radios and is not linked into anything we ship.

Why this tree: the AOSP mirror (Cuttlefish) is the most complete copy —
upstream github.com/bcopeland/wmediumd stops at 717e5d7 (2021-03-01), and
AOSP carries three more years of fixes (frame bit rates, PMSR, gRPC control).

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (wmediumd.c, config.c, per.c, pmsr.c, list.h);
BSD-3-Clause (lib/, inc/usfstl). Not vendored for that reason — build.sh
fetches this commit and applies patches/; the repo carries only this file,
the patches and the script. Patches touching GPL files are GPL-2.0-or-later.

Built: wmediumd/ with its Makefile. Not built: main.cc and wmediumd_server/
(C++, android-base, gRPC), Android.bp, util/, tests/.

Patches:
  0001-plain-c-main-and-pmsr.patch  C main() equivalent to main.cc without
                                    the gRPC server; pmsr.o added to OBJECTS
                                    (the AOSP Makefile does not link otherwise)
